and context, the Magister audit, and the marketing plan, and ask me to pick one.\n3. Write the full draft here in chat — title, slug, meta description, and body in the repository's format — and ask for my approval.\n4. Only after I approve: create a branch, commit the post, and open a pull request with a clear description. Never merge it, and never push to the default branch directly.\n",`Creating the branch and pull request goes through Magister's approval flow; do not bypass it. ${Q}`].join("\n")}}},{key:"vercel_deployment_review",services:["vercel"],rank:"single",writes:!1,icon:K.Rocket,eligible:e=>(q(e,"vercel")?.resources.length??0)>0,build:e=>{let t=X(W(q(e,"vercel")));return{title:t?`Review recent deployment health for ${t}`:"Review recent deployment health",subtitle:"Failed builds, slow deploys, and likely production risks from your connected Vercel project — read-only.",brandMatch:!1,prompt:["Review the recent deployment health of the connected Vercel project.\n",Y,"",ee(t,"Vercel project",!1),"\nThen:\n1. List the last 20 deployments with their state, target (production or preview), duration, and commit or branch.\n2. For any failed or errored deployment, read the build logs and summarize the cause in plain language.\n3. Flag likely production risks: repeated failures, unusually long builds, or a production deployment older than recent commits.\n4. Recommend what to fix first and what to monitor.\n","This is a read-only review: do not redeploy, roll back, change environment variables, or touch domains. "+Q].join("\n")}}},{key:"wix_blog_draft",services:["wix"],rank:"single",writes:!0,icon:g.PenLine,eligible:e=>(q(e,"wix")?.resources.length??0)>0,build:e=>{let t=X(W(q(e,"wix")));return{title:t?`Draft the next post for ${t}`:"Draft the next blog post for your Wix site",subtitle:"Read what the site already publishes, draft a post that fits, and stage it as a Wix draft for your approval.",brandMatch:!1,prompt:["Draft the next blog post for the connected Wix sit